# Playbook

Example of playbook.md: your rules for the CoS and leads, part of their system prompts.
Copy it to playbook.md beside this file and make it yours (`fleet init` seeds one if none
exists). One rule per line, newest last; the CoS appends one only after you approve it.
Which program and login each role uses is in the fleet skill's roles.json, not here.

## Always ask me
- Merging to a production branch, deploying, deleting anything remote, spending money.

## Learned
- Leads may merge to dev once a human reviewer approved and required checks pass (approved 2026-01-15).

## Worktrees
- Every agent that changes code works in its own worktree from `wt new <repo>/<project>-<slug>`, never in a repo's main checkout. `wt info <repo>` (or `--all`) says where it lives and how to boot it (the `worktrees` skill).
